        "original_id": "5f05c313-30ab-51f3-ae75-611a5f1ee3cb",
        "text": "This chunk compares emus and ostriches as large living ratite birds.\n\nThis chunk is about:\n- Animals: emu, common ostrich\n- Taxonomy: Dromaius novaehollandiae, Struthio camelus, Struthio, ratites\n- Places: Africa\n\nFacts:\n- The emu is Dromaius novaehollandiae.\n- The emu is the second-largest living bird by height after the ostrich.\n- The emu is a ratite relative of the ostrich.\n- The common ostrich is Struthio camelus.\n- The ostrich or common ostrich is one or possibly two species of large flightless birds native to Africa.\n- The ostrich is the only living member or members of the genus Struthio, which belongs to the ratite family.",
